course: dictionary
lesson: 1276
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Bustle can be a noun (a thing or an activity) or a verb (an action). Read the words around it to decide.
explain: As a noun, bustle means busy, noisy activity with lots of people moving about: «the hustle and bustle of the city». As a verb, it means to move around quickly and busily, like a cook who bustles about the kitchen.
explain: In «Bustle about, old chap!», bustle is a verb. It tells someone to move around quickly and get busy. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or an action? That question will often point you to the right meaning.
fact: Bustle (noun) means busy, noisy activity with lots of people moving about.
fact: Bustle (verb) means to move around quickly and busily.
fact: In the 1800s, a bustle was a pad or frame worn under the back of a long skirt to make it puff out.
fact: The phrase «hustle and bustle» means lots of busy, noisy activity.
exercise: What does bustle mean in «the hustle and bustle of the city»? | A quiet walk in the park | A pad worn under a long skirt | A type of bus | *Busy, noisy activity with lots of people moving about
exercise: What does «Bustle about, old chap!» ask someone to do? | Sit down and rest | Go to sleep early | *Move around quickly and busily | Speak very softly
exercise: In history lessons on Victorian clothes, what was a bustle? | A pair of leather boots | A kind of long coat | A hat with a wide brim | *A pad or frame worn under the back of a long skirt
test: The market was full of bustle on Saturday morning. What does bustle mean here? | Silence and calm | A type of market stall | *Busy, noisy activity with lots of people moving about | A frame worn under a skirt
test: Which word in «Bustle about, old chap!» is the verb? | old | about | *Bustle | chap
exam: In the phrase «the hustle and bustle of the city», bustle means | a short journey by bus | a pad worn under a long skirt | *busy, noisy activity | a quiet, empty street
